<title>USA: LaserVision optimistic on new revenues.</title>
<headline>LaserVision optimistic on new revenues.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>LaserVision Centers Inc said on Friday it expects sales to continue to improve as its fleet of lasers continue to be redeployed after being idled during the third quarter ended January 31.</p>
<p>The company, which makes lasers used in eye surgery, earlier reported a loss of $2.3 million, or $0.26 a share, in the period compared to a loss of $1.6 million, or $0.32, a year ago. Total revenues reached $2.0 million, up from $852,000, the company said.</p>
<p>LaserVision said it has about 100 contracts pending.</p>
<p>Its shares closed unchanged Friday at 5-7/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
